r swimming in fresh water with an open wound", "strength": "weak"}], "comorbidities": ["Diabetes mellitus", "Chronic venous insufficiency", "Lymphedema", "Peripheral arterial disease", "Immunosuppression", "Cirrhosis", "Chronic kidney disease", "Heart failure"], "family_history": [], "social_history": ["Injection drug use", "Occupations with skin trauma such as farming or construction", "Homelessness or crowded living conditions"], "exposures": ["Recent insect bite", "Recent skin wound or abrasion", "Recent surgery", "Animal bite", "Fresh water exposure with an open wound"], "risk_medications": ["prednisone", "methotrexate", "tacrolimus", "cyclosporine", "infliximab", "adalimumab"]}, "presentation": {"chief_complaints": [{"text": "My leg is red, swollen, and hurts", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "The redness is spreading", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "I feel hot and achy", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "My arm is red and tender", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "hpi": {"onset": "Fairly rapid, over 1–3 days; often the patient can point to a bite, scrape, or crack in the skin that came first", "duration": "Usually 1–4 days at presentation", "progression": "The area of redness and swelling enlarges steadily; pain and warmth increase; fever and chills may develop as it spreads", "location": "Most often the lower leg, but can be the arm, face, or any site of skin breakdown", "radiation": "No radiation; the process spreads locally rather than following a nerve", "quality": "Burning, throbbing, and tender to the touch; the skin feels tight and hot", "severity": "Moderate; pain is often 4–7/10 and worse with standing or walking", "timing": "Constant, gradually worsening", "aggravating": ["Standing or walking on the affected leg", "Touching or pressing the area", "Tight clothing or shoes"], "relieving": ["Elevating the limb", "Resting", "Acetaminophen or ibuprofen"], "associated_symptoms": [{"text": "Fever", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Chills", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Swollen or tender lymph nodes near the area", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Feeling generally unwell or achy", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "A red streak running up the limb", "frequency": "rare"}, {"text": "Clear or pus-filled drainage from the wound", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Nausea", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "pertinent_negatives": ["Pain out of proportion to the exam or rapidly worsening pain", "Skin turning dusky, gray, or black", "Crepitus or crackling under the skin", "Numbness or loss of sensation in the area", "Severe pain with light touch out of keeping with the redness", "Recent long flight or immobility with calf pain", "Joint swelling with inability to bear weight", "Recurrent boils or draining sinus tracts"]}, "ros": [{"system": "constitutional", "positives": [{"text": "Fever", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Chills", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Fatigue or feeling unwell", "frequency": "common"}], "negatives": ["Weight loss", "Night sweats"]}, {"system": "skin", "positives": [{"text": "Red, warm, swollen area of skin", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "Tenderness to touch", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "A break in the skin, bite, or scrape at the edge of the redness", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Blisters or peeling skin over the red area", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Drainage or pus from the wound", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Black or dead-looking skin", "Skin cracking or popping when pressed", "Multiple draining boils", "Rash on both legs in the same pattern"], "argues_against": ["Necrotizing soft tissue infection", "Stasis dermatitis"]}, {"system": "musculoskeletal", "positives": [{"text": "Limb swelling", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Pain with movement of the nearby joint", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Joint locked or unable to bear weight", "Muscle weakness out of proportion to pain"], "argues_against": ["Septic arthritis", "Deep vein thrombosis"]}, {"system": "hematologic", "positives": [{"text": "Tender lymph nodes near the area", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Easy bruising or bleeding", "Blood clots in the legs"]}, {"system": "gastrointestinal", "positives": [{"text": "Nausea", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Vomiting", "Abdominal pain"]}, {"system": "neurologic", "positives": [], "negatives": ["Numbness or tingling in the affected limb", "Confusion", "Severe pain out of proportion to exam"], "argues_against": ["Necrotizing soft tissue infection", "Sepsis with altered mental status"]}], "atypical": [{"population": "older_adults", "how_it_differs": "May have little or no fever and less pain; redness can be mistaken for chronic venous changes, and they can become confused or hypotensive quickly.", "missing_classic_features": ["Fever", "Marked pain"]}, {"population": "diabetes", "how_it_differs": "Often presents with a foot ulcer or a deeper, less obvious infection; neuropathy can blunt pain and the redness may be less striking.", "missing_classic_features": ["Prominent pain", "Clear area of spreading redness"]}, {"population": "immunocompromised", "how_it_differs": "Can progress faster and with fewer local signs; fever may be the main clue and unusual organisms are more likely.", "missing_classic_features": ["Marked local warmth and redness"]}, {"population": "children", "how_it_differs": "Often follows an insect bite or minor trauma; the child may refuse to walk or use the limb and may be fussy rather than describing pain.", "missing_classic_features": ["Clear description of spreading redness"]}, {"population": "infants", "how_it_differs": "Presents with irritability, poor feeding, and fever; the skin finding may be subtle or on the diaper area.", "missing_classic_features": ["Localized pain report", "Obvious redness"]}, {"population": "pregnancy", "how_it_differs": "Lower leg swelling is common in pregnancy, so cellulitis can be mistaken for normal swelling; redness and warmth help distinguish it.", "missing_classic_features": ["Clear asymmetry of the legs"]}, {"population": "obesity", "how_it_differs": "Skin folds and leg swelling make the redness harder to see and the area harder to examine; recurrent episodes are more common.", "missing_classic_features": ["Easy visualization of the affected area"]}, {"population": "renal_impairment", "how_it_differs": "Fluid overload and chronic skin changes can mask or mimic cellulitis; antibiotic dosing needs adjustment.", "missing_classic_features": ["Sharp demarcation of redness"]}]}, "exam": {"general": {"mild": "Well-appearing, comfortable at rest, no distress", "moderate": "Mildly ill-appearing, favors the affected limb, uncomfortable with movement", "severe": "Ill-appearing, flushed, tachycardic, reluctant to move the limb", "critical": "Toxic-appearing, pale or mottled, diaphoretic, may be confused or lethargic"}, "findings": [{"id": "erythema", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Inspect the affected area in good light, comparing with the opposite limb", "finding": "Diffuse, poorly demarcated area of erythema", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "strongly_supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "warmth", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Palpate the red area and compare with the unaffected side", "finding": "Increased warmth of the involved skin", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "strongly_supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "tenderness", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Gently palpate the involved area", "finding": "Tenderness to palpation", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "edema", "region": "extremities", "maneuver": "Inspect and palpate the limb for swelling, comparing sides", "finding": "Localized swelling or pitting edema of the affected limb", "frequency": "common", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "skin-break", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Search