m"}, {"question": "Have you coughed up any blood?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Hemoptysis suggests pulmonary embolism or pneumonia"}, {"question": "Have you fainted or felt like you might pass out?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Syncope or near-syncope suggests a high-risk cause such as arrhythmia, massive pulmonary embolism, or dissection"}, {"question": "Do you have any leg swelling or calf pain?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Unilateral leg swelling or calf tenderness suggests deep vein thrombosis with pulmonary embolism"}, {"question": "Have you had any recent surgery, hospitalization, long travel, or immobilization?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Recent surgery, hospitalization, long travel, or immobilization raises venous thromboembolism risk and points toward pulmonary embolism"}, {"question": "Do you have a history of heart disease, heart attack, diabetes, high blood pressure, or high cholesterol?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Coronary risk factors raise the pretest probability of acute coronary syndrome"}, {"question": "Have you had a blood clot in your leg or lung before, or do you have cancer?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Prior venous thromboembolism or active cancer raises pulmonary embolism risk"}, {"question": "Do you have reflux or heartburn, and does food or lying down bring on the pain?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Known reflux with postprandial or positional burning pain suggests a gastrointestinal cause"}, {"question": "Do you take birth control pills, hormone replacement, or any stimulants such as cocaine or amphetamines?", "category": "medications", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Estrogen-containing contraceptives and hormone therapy raise venous thromboembolism risk; cocaine and