ery, immobilization, long travel, active cancer, and prior venous thromboembolism", "Considers the broad differential including acute coronary syndrome, pulmonary embolism, aortic dissection, pericarditis, pneumothorax, pneumonia, reflux, costochondritis, and panic attack", "Recognizes that reproducible chest wall tenderness does not fully exclude a cardiac cause", "Orders an ECG within 10 minutes of arrival when acute coronary syndrome is suspected", "Uses serial high-sensitivity troponin testing rather than a single value to detect acute myocardial injury", "Confirms pregnancy status before imaging or medications that are contraindicated in pregnancy", "Does not delay reperfusion for a patient with ST-segment elevation on ECG"], "difficulty": {"easy": ["Classic substernal pressure with exertion, radiation to the left arm or jaw, and diaphoresis in a patient with coronary risk factors", "Sudden pleuritic pain with dyspnea and tachycardia after recent surgery or long travel", "Sharp positional pain that improves leaning forward with a pericardial friction rub after a viral illness", "Burning postprandial pain relieved by antacids in a younger patient without coronary risk factors"], "medium": ["Older adult with dyspnea and weakness but no classic chest pain", "Patient with diabetes and blunted anginal pain presenting with dyspnea alone", "Reproducible chest wall tenderness in a patient who also has coronary risk factors", "Pleuritic pain with clear lungs and no dyspnea where pulmonary embolism and musculoskeletal causes compete", "Young woman with chest tightness, palpitations, and anxiety where panic attack and coronary causes compete"], "hard": ["Sudden tearing pain maximal at onset radiating to the back with a blood pressure differential between arms", "Hypotension with distended neck veins and unilateral absent breath sounds", "Chest pain with syncope or near-syncope suggesting arrhythmia, massive pulmonary embolism, or dissection", "Pregnant patient with pleuri