e yet", "differential lung-cancer: no profile yet", "differential bronchiectasis: no profile yet", "differential tuberculosis: no profile yet", "differential upper-airway-cough-syndrome: no profile yet", "differential gastroesophageal-reflux-disease: no profile yet", "differential alpha-1-antitrypsin-deficiency: no profile yet"]}, "review": {"status": "pending"}}, "patient": {"age": {"typical_min": 40, "typical_max": 80, "peak": "50–70", "possible_min": 25, "possible_max": 95}, "sex": "either", "demographics": ["More common in people with a long smoking history", "In the US, prevalence is higher among adults with lower income and less education", "Slightly more common in men, largely reflecting historical smoking patterns"], "risk_factors": [{"text": "Current or former cigarette smoking", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "Long-term exposure to secondhand smoke", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Occupational exposure to dusts, fumes, or chemical vapors", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Long-term exposure to air pollution", "strength": "weak"}, {"text": "Family history of COPD in a smoker", "strength": "weak"}, {"text": "Alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency", "strength": "weak"}], "comorbidities": ["Emphysema (often coexists)", "Asthma", "Coronary artery disease", "Heart failure", "Gastroesophageal reflux disease", "Obstructive sleep apnea", "Anxiety or depression", "Osteoporosis"], "family_history": ["COPD in a first-degree relative", "Alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency"], "social_history": ["Cigarette smoking, often 20 or more pack-years", "Exposure to secondhand smoke at home or work", "Work in mining, construction, manufacturing, farming, or other dusty trades"], "exposures": ["Cigarette smoke", "Pipe or cigar smoke", "Secondhand smoke", "Wood or biomass smoke", "Dusts and fumes at work", "Air pollution"], "risk_medications": []}, "presentation": {"chief_complaints": [{"text": "I've had a cough with phlegm for months and it won't go away", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "I get winded just walking up the stairs", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "I keep getting chest colds", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "My chest feels tight and I wheeze", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "hpi": {"onset": "Gradual, over years; most people first notice the cough in their 40s or later", "duration": "Cough and sputum on most days for at least 3 months a year, for 2 years or more", "progression": "Slowly worsening; cough and sputum come first, then breathlessness with activity, then breathlessness with minimal activity as the disease advances", "location": "Chest", "quality": "Loose, rattling cough that brings up sputum; chest tightness; breathlessness on exertion", "severity": "Mild at first and easy to dismiss as a 'smoker's cough'; becomes moderate to severe over years", "timing": "Cough is worst in the morning right after waking and when lying down; symptoms are worse in cold air and during respiratory infections", "aggravating": ["Cold air", "Exercise or climbing stairs", "Respiratory infections", "Smoke, dust, fumes, or strong odors", "Lying flat"], "relieving": ["Coughing up the sputum", "Resting", "Sitting upright", "Inhaled bronchodilator (partial relief)"], "associated_symptoms": [{"text": "Cough that brings up clear, white, or gray sputum", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "Shortness of breath with activity", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Wheezing or a whistling sound when breathing", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Chest tightness", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Frequent colds or chest infections", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Sputum that turns yellow or green during flare-ups", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Low energy or fatigue", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Waking at night coughing or short of breath", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Ankle or leg swelling in advanced disease", "frequency": "rare"}, {"text": "Unintentional weight loss in advanced disease", "frequency": "rare"}], "pertinent_negatives": ["Coughing up blood", "Fever with the chronic cough between flare-ups", "Night sweats", "Sudden severe shortness of breath at rest", "Sharp chest pain that worsens with a deep breath", "Leg pain or swelling in one calf only", "Weight loss before the illness became severe", "New wheezing that started in childhood or as a young adult", "Symptoms that began suddenly over hours to days"]}, "ros": [{"system": "respiratory", "positives": [{"text": "Chronic productive cough", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "Sputum production most days", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "Shortness of breath with exertion", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Wheezing", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Chest tightness", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Frequent respiratory infections", "frequency": "common"}], "negatives": ["Hemoptysis", "Pleuritic chest pain", "Sudden severe dyspnea at rest"], "argues_against": ["Lung cancer", "Pulmonary embolism", "Pneumothorax"]}, {"system": "constitutional", "positives": [{"text": "Fatigue", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Low-grade fever during flare-ups only", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Weight loss", "Night sweats", "Fever between flare-ups"], "argues_against": ["Tuberculosis", "Malignancy", "Chronic infection"]}, {"system": "cardiovascular", "positives": [{"text": "Ankle or leg swelling in advanced disease", "frequency": "rare"}], "negatives": ["Chest pain with exertion", "Palpitations", "Orthopnea", "Paroxysmal nocturnal dyspnea", "Unilateral leg swelling"], "argues_against": ["Heart failure as the primary cause", "Deep vein thrombosis"]}, {"system": "ent", "positives": [{"text": "Throat clearing from postnasal drip", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Chronic nasal congestion", "Recurrent sinus infections"], "argues_against": ["Upper airway cough syndrome"]}, {"system": "gastrointestinal", "positives": [{"text": "Heartburn", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Regurgitation", "Difficulty swallowing", "Vomiting"], "argues_against": ["Gastroesophageal reflux as the sole cause of cough"]}, {"system": "musculoskeletal", "positives": [{"text": "Muscle aches from coughing", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Chest wall tenderness", "Rib pain at rest"], "argues_against": ["Costochondritis", "Rib fracture"]}, {"system": "psychiatric", "positives": [{"text": "Anxiety about breathing", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Low mood", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Suicidal ideation"]}], "atypical": [{"population": "older_adults", "how_it_differs": "Symptoms may be attributed to 'just getting older' or to heart disease, and activity limitation may be the main complaint rather than cough.", "missing_classic_features": ["Prominent sputum production", "Reported wheezing"]}, {"population": "children", "how_it_differs": "Chronic bronchitis is uncommon in children; a chronic productive cough in a child should prompt evaluation for asthma, cystic fibrosis, or recurrent aspiration instead.", "missing_classic_features": ["Long smoking history", "Typical adult age of onset"]}, {"population": "pregnancy", "how_it_differs": "Increasing shortness of breath may be attributed to normal pregnancy changes, delaying recognition of worsening lung disease.", "missing_classic_features": ["Clear temporal link to smoking history"]}, {"population": "immunocompromised", "how_it_differs": "Recurrent chest infections may dominate the picture and the chronic cough may be attributed to infection rather than underlying airway disease.", "missing_classic_features": ["Stable chronic sputum pattern"]}]}, "exam": {"general": {"mild": "Comfortable at rest, speaks in full sentences, no distress", "moderate": "Speaks in full sentences but pauses to breathe when walking or climbing; mild tachypnea", "severe": "Sits upright, pursed-lip breathing, uses accessory muscles, speaks in short phrases", "critical": "Ill-appearing, tripod position, unable to speak in full sentences, ma