; hemodynamic instability; requires noninvasive or invasive ventilation"}, "red_flags": [{"finding": "Acidemia on arterial blood gas in a patient with known CO2 retention", "meaning": "Acute-on-chronic respiratory failure; needs urgent ventilatory support"}, {"finding": "Altered mental status, somnolence, or asterixis", "meaning": "Hypercapnic encephalopathy; impending respiratory failure"}, {"finding": "SpO2 below 88% on room air or new oxygen requirement", "meaning": "Severe hypoxemia; assess for pneumonia, pulmonary embolism, or pneumothorax"}, {"finding": "Hemoptysis", "meaning": "Consider lung cancer, bronchiectasis, or tuberculosis rather than uncomplicated chronic bronchitis"}, {"finding": "Unilateral leg swelling or pleuritic chest pain", "meaning": "Pulmonary embolism until proven otherwise"}, {"finding": "Sudden unilateral pleuritic pain with absent breath sounds", "meaning": "Pneumothorax, which is more common in patients with emphysema"}, {"finding": "Fever with purulent sputum and worsening dyspnea", "meaning": "Acute bacterial exacerbation or pneumonia; needs antibiotics and possibly hospitalization"}, {"finding": "New focal wheeze or focal crackles", "meaning": "Consider endobronchial obstruction from a mass or a retained foreign body"}], "complications": [{"name": "Acute exacerbation of COPD", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "common", "clues": ["Increased sputum volume or purulence", "Worsening dyspnea", "Increased cough and wheeze", "Low-grade fever"]}, {"name": "Acute respiratory failure with hypercapnia", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "life_threatening", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Drowsiness or confusion", "Accessory muscle use", "SpO2 below 88%", "Acidemia on arterial blood gas"]}, {"name": "Bacterial pneumonia", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["High fever", "Focal crackles or consolidation", "Leukocytosis", "New infiltrate on chest x-ray"]}, {"name": "Cor pulmonal