isease. Consider atypical organisms and evaluate for bronchiectasis."}, {"population": "obesity", "differences": "Reduced chest wall compliance and deconditioning worsen dyspnea; obesity hypoventilation can add to CO2 retention and complicate interpretation of blood gases."}, {"population": "diabetes", "differences": "Systemic corticosteroids used during exacerbations cause hyperglycemia; monitor glucose closely and adjust therapy."}]}, "teaching": {"key_questions": [{"question": "How long have you had this cough, and does it bring up phlegm?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Productive cough on most days for at least 3 months a year for 2 or more years"}, {"question": "Is the cough there every day, or does it come and go?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Chronic daily pattern rather than episodic attacks with symptom-free intervals"}, {"question": "When during the day is the cough worst?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Worst in the morning after waking and when lying down"}, {"question": "What does the sputum look like?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Clear, white, or gray most days; yellow or green during flare-ups"}, {"question": "Do you get short of breath? With what level of activity?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Exertional dyspnea that has crept in after years of cough; grades activity tolerance"}, {"question": "Do you smoke or have you ever smoked? How much and for how many years?", "category": "social", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Current or former cigarette use, often 20 or more pack-years"}, {"question": "Have you been exposed to dusts, fumes, or chemicals at work, or to secondhand smoke at home?", "category": "social", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Occupational or household inhaled irritants that add to the smoking risk"}, {"question": "Have you coughed up any blood?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Absent; hemoptysis points to cancer, bronchiectasis, or tuberculosis"}, {"question": "Have you lost weight without trying, or had night sweats or fevers between flare-ups?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Absent; present suggests malignancy, tuberculosis, or another chronic infection"}, {"question": "Do you wake up at night short of breath, or need extra pillows to sleep?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Absent; orthopnea and paroxysmal nocturnal dyspnea point to heart failure"}, {"question": "Have you noticed swelling in your ankles or legs?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Bilateral swelling in advanced disease suggests cor pulmonale; one-sided swelling suggests DVT"}, {"question": "How many chest colds or flare-ups have you had in the past year, and have you needed antibiotics or steroids?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Frequent exacerbations, which drive management and prognosis"}, {"question": "What inhalers or other breathing medicines do you use, and do they help?", "category": "medications", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Bronchodilator use with partial relief; steroid inhalers in more severe disease"}, {"question": "Have you had your flu and pneumococcal vaccines?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "optional", "looking_for": "Up-to-date immunizations, which reduce exacerbations"}, {"question": "Does anyone in your family have COPD, emphysema, or liver disease at a young age?", "category": "family", "importance": "optional", "looking_for": "Family history suggesting alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency"}, {"question": "Has your cough changed recently, or is it worse than it has ever been?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "A change in a stable chronic pattern, which should prompt evaluation for a new problem"}], "accepted_names": ["Chronic bronchitis", "COPD with chronic bronchitis", "Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, bronchitis-predominant", "Type B COPD", "COPD, chronic bronchitis phenotype"], "reasoning_points": ["Productive cough on most days for at least 3 months a year for 2 consecutive years", "Other causes of chronic cough excluded (asthma, upper airway cough syndrome, reflux, infection, malignancy)", "Long-term cigarette smoke exposure, often 20 or more pack-years", "Typical age of onset in the 40s or later, with gradual worsening over years", "Cough worst in the morning and with cold air or infections", "Spirometry showing persistent post-bronchodilator airflow obstruction with FEV1/FVC below 0.70", "Chest imaging without a mass, infiltrate, or other alternative explanation", "No hemoptysis, weight loss, night sweats, or fever between flare-ups"], "difficulty": {"easy": ["Long-time smoker over 40 with a daily morning productive cough for years", "Sputum is clear to white and worse in the morning", "Diffuse expiratory wheezing and a prolonged expiratory phase on exam", "Spirometry shows post-bronchodilator FEV1/FVC below 0.70"], "medium": ["Patient dismisses the cough as a 'smoker's cough' and reports only exertional dyspnea", "Coexisting heart failure or asthma makes the cause of dyspnea ambiguous", "Older adult whose activity limitation is attributed to aging", "Chest x-ray is normal, which does not exclude the diagnosis"], "hard": ["Younger patient or one with minimal smoking history, raising concern for alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency", "Chronic cough with purulent sputum and recurrent same-lobe pneumonias suggesting bronchiectasis", "Smoker with hemoptysis or weight loss requiring evaluation for lung cancer", "Acute-on-chronic presentation with hypercapnia and acidemia obscuring the underlying chronic disease", "Immunocompromised patient whose recurrent infections dominate the picture"]}}}$rounds_kb$::jsonb)
