ial", "looking_for": "Gradual onset over 1–3 days; worsening breathlessness around days 5–10 suggests severe disease"}, {"question": "Have you been in close contact with anyone who has COVID-19, or been in a crowded indoor setting without a mask?", "category": "social", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Household member, workplace outbreak, or indoor gathering with a known case"}, {"question": "Have you lost your sense of smell or taste?", "category": "associated", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "New loss of smell or taste strongly supports COVID-19 over other viral illnesses"}, {"question": "Do you have a fever, chills, or night sweats?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Fever with chills, often spiking in the late afternoon and evening"}, {"question": "Are you coughing? Is it dry or are you bringing anything up?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Dry or minimally productive cough; thick colored sputum suggests bacterial superinfection"}, {"question": "Are you short of breath? Does it happen at rest or only with exertion?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Dyspnea at rest or with minimal exertion marks moderate or worse disease"}, {"question": "How far can you walk before you have to stop and catch your breath?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Declining exercise tolerance; walking to the bathroom and getting winded is a red flag"}, {"question": "Do you have any muscle aches, headache, or sore throat?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Common constitutional symptoms supporting a viral syndrome"}, {"question": "Any nausea, vomiting, or diarrhea?", "category": "associated", "importance": "optional", "looking_for": "GI symptoms sometimes occur and can be the presenting complaint"}, {"question": "Have you had any chest pain or palpitations?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Pleuritic pain or chest pressure raises concern for pulmonary embolism or myocarditis"}, {"question": "Have you been confused or had trouble concentrating?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "New confusion, especially in older adults, is a red flag for severe disease"}, {"question": "Have you been vaccinated against COVID-19, and when was your last dose or prior infection?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "No prior vaccination or infection increases risk of severe disease"}, {"question": "Do you have diabetes, lung disease, heart disease, kidney disease, or a weakened immune system?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Comorbidities that raise the risk of severe disease and change disposition"}, {"question": "Do you take any medications that suppress the immune system, like prednisone or tacrolimus?", "category": "medications", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Immunosuppressive medications increase risk of severe or prolonged disease"}, {"question": "Do you live in a nursing home, shelter, or other group setting?", "category": "social", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Congregate living increases exposure risk and risk of severe disease"}, {"question": "Do you smoke?", "category": "social", "importance": "optional", "looking_for": "Tobacco use increases respiratory risk"}, {"question": "Could you be pregnant?", "category": "obstetric", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Pregnancy increases risk of severe disease and preterm birth"}], "accepted_names": ["COVID-19", "Coronavirus disease 2019", "SARS-CoV-2 infection", "COVID"], "reasoning_points": ["Gradual onset over 1–3 days of fever, dry cough, fatigue, and myalgias", "New loss of smell or taste strongly supports COVID-19 over other viral illnesses", "Close contact with a known case or indoor crowded gathering without masks", "Risk factors such as age 65 or older, obesity, diabetes, 