ng vertigo; a low value points away from a vestibular cause."}, {"test_id": "glucose", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 55, "max": 69}, "moderate": {"min": 45, "max": 54}, "severe": {"min": 35, "max": 44}, "critical": {"min": 20, "max": 34}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "essential", "caveat": "Hypoglycemia is a reversible cause of lightheadedness, sweating and confusion; check it at the bedside in any patient on insulin or a sulfonylurea."}, {"test_id": "tsh", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 4.5, "max": 8.0}, "moderate": {"min": 8.0, "max": 15.0}, "severe": {"min": 15.0, "max": 40.0}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Both hypothyroidism and hyperthyroidism can cause dizziness; a suppressed TSH with high free T4 suggests hyperthyroidism."}, {"test_id": "na", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 130, "max": 134}, "moderate": {"min": 125, "max": 129}, "severe": {"min": 118, "max": 124}, "critical": {"min": 105, "max": 117}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Hyponatremia from thiazides or SIADH causes confusion, unsteadiness and lightheadedness."}, {"test_id": "cr", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 1.2, "max": 1.6}, "moderate": {"min": 1.6, "max": 2.5}, "severe": {"min": 2.5, "max": 4.5}, "critical": {"min": 4.5, "max": 9.0}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Elevated creatinine suggests dehydration or kidney injury, which can cause orthostatic dizziness and limits medication choices."}, {"test_id": "bun", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 21, "max": 30}, "moderate": {"min": 30, "max": 45}, "severe": {"min": 45, "max": 70}, "critical": {"min": 70, "max": 120}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "A BUN-to-creatinine ratio above 20 supports dehydration as a contributor to orthostatic dizziness."}, {"test_id": "hcg", "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "essential", "caveat": "Check in anyone of childbearing age before imaging or medication changes; a positive result changes the differential and the imaging plan."}, {"test_id": "wbc", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 11.0, "max": 14.0}, "moderate": {"min": 14.0, "max": 18.0}, "severe": {"min": 18.0, "max": 25.0}, "critical": {"min": 25.0, "max": 40.0}}, "frequency": "rare", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "A high white count with fever and neck stiffness raises concern for meningitis or a central nervous system infection."}, {"test_id": "crp", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 1.0, "max": 3.0}, "moderate": {"min": 3.0, "max": 8.0}, "severe": {"min": 8.0, "max": 20.0}, "critical": {"min": 20.0, "max": 40.0}}, "frequency": "rare", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Nonspecific; a marked rise with fever suggests infection such as meningitis or mastoiditis."}, {"test_id": "esr", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 21, "max": 40}, "moderate": {"min": 40, "max": 70}, "severe": {"min": 70, "max": 100}, "critical": {"min": 100, "max": 130}}, "frequency": "rare", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Very high values in an older adult with headache and jaw claudication suggest giant cell arteritis."}, {"test_id": "b12", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 150, "max": 199}, "moderate": {"min": 100, "max": 149}, "severe": {"min": 50, "max": 99}, "critical": {"min": 20, "max": 49}}, "frequency": "rare", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Deficiency causes sensory ataxia and unsteadiness, especially in older adults and after gastric surgery."}, {"test_id": "a1c", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 5.7, "max": 6.4}, "moderate": {"min": 6.5, "max": 8.0}, "severe": {"min": 8.0, "max": 10.0}, "critical": {"min": 10.0, "max": 14.0}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Poorly controlled diabetes raises the odds of autonomic neuropathy causing orthostatic dizziness."}], "ecg": {"findings": [{"feature": "rhythm", "finding": "Atrial fibrillation with irregularly irregular ventricular response", "frequency": "sometimes", "min_severity": "moderate"}, {"feature": "rhythm", "finding": "Sinus bradycardia", "frequ