al flutter with a rapid or slow ventricular response", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"feature": "rhythm", "finding": "Sinus bradycardia", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"feature": "rhythm", "finding": "Ventricular tachycardia or other wide-complex tachycardia", "frequency": "rare"}, {"feature": "rate", "finding": "Heart rate under 50 beats per minute", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"feature": "rate", "finding": "Heart rate over 150 beats per minute", "frequency": "rare"}, {"feature": "pr", "finding": "Prolonged PR interval (first-degree AV block)", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"feature": "pr", "finding": "Progressively lengthening PR then a dropped QRS (second-degree AV block, Mobitz I)", "frequency": "rare"}, {"feature": "pr", "finding": "Intermittent dropped QRS without PR lengthening (Mobitz II) or complete AV block", "frequency": "rare"}, {"feature": "qrs", "finding": "Widened QRS over 120 ms", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"feature": "qrs", "finding": "Left ventricular hypertrophy by voltage criteria", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"feature": "qt", "finding": "Prolonged QTc over 480 ms", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"feature": "qt", "finding": "Short QTc under 340 ms (short QT syndrome)", "frequency": "rare"}, {"feature": "st", "finding": "ST elevation or depression suggesting acute myocardial ischemia or infarction", "frequency": "rare"}, {"feature": "t_wave", "finding": "T-wave inversion in precordial leads", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"feature": "other", "finding": "Epsilon wave or T-wave inversion in V1 to V3 (arrhythmogenic right ventricular cardiomyopathy)", "frequency": "rare"}, {"feature": "other", "finding": "Brugada pattern with coved ST elevation in V1 to V2", "frequency": "rare"}, {"feature": "other", "finding": "Pacemaker spikes or an implanted defibrillator", "frequency": "rare"}]}, "imaging": [{"study": "Echocardiogram, transthoracic", "modality": "echo", "preferred_when": "Suspected structural heart disease, murmur, exertional fainting, or abnormal ECG", "findings": [{"text": "Normal chamber size and function", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Aortic stenosis with a thickened, restricted aortic valve", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Left ventricular hypertrophy with asymmetric septal thickening (hypertrophic cardiomyopathy)", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Reduced left ventricular ejection fraction", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Right ventricular dilation with reduced function (arrhythmogenic right ventricular cardiomyopathy)", "frequency": "rare"}, {"text": "Intracardiac mass such as an atrial myxoma", "frequency": "rare"}, {"text": "Pericardial effusion", "frequency": "rare"}]}, {"study": "CT head without contrast", "modality": "ct", "preferred_when": "Head trauma from the fall, focal neurologic findings, or persistent altered mental status", "findings": [{"text": "No acute intracranial abnormality", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Intracranial hemorrhage such as subdural or subarachnoid blood", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Skull fracture", "frequency": "rare"}]}, {"study": "MRI brain with and without contrast", "modality": "mri", "preferred_when": "Focal neurologic deficits or suspected seizure or structural brain lesion", "findings": [{"text": "No acute abnormality", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Cortical or hippocampal signal change suggesting seizure", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Mass lesion or stroke", "frequency": "rare"}]}, {"study": "CT pulmonary angiogram", "modality": "ct", "preferred_when": "Suspected pulmonary embolism with tachycardia, hypoxemia, or pleuritic chest pain", "findings": [{"text": "Filling defect in the pulmonary arteries", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Right ventricular enlargement", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "No pulmonary embolism", "frequency": "common"}]}, {"study": "Chest x-ray", "modality": "xray", "preferred_when": "Dyspnea, chest pain, or suspected cardiac or pulmonary cause", "findings": [{"text": "Normal heart size and clea