evated shortly after a generalized seizure"], "imaging": ["MRI brain may show cortical or hippocampal signal change", "CT head if trauma or acute intracranial cause is suspected"]}}, {"name": "Hypoglycemia", "slug": "hypoglycemia", "why_considered": "Low blood sugar causes lightheadedness, sweating, confusion, and loss of consciousness.", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Diabetes, insulin or sulfonylurea use, or altered mental status that improves with glucose", "discriminators": {"history": ["Diabetes with insulin or sulfonylurea use", "Missed meal or excessive exercise", "Symptoms improve quickly with sugar or food", "No clear positional or emotional trigger"], "exam": ["Diaphoresis, tremor, or confusion", "Symptoms resolve after glucose administration"], "labs": ["Low bedside glucose", "Low serum glucose with symptoms that resolve after correction"]}}, {"name": "Orthostatic hypotension", "slug": "orthostatic-hypotension", "why_considered": "A drop in blood pressure on standing causes lightheadedness and fainting, often with a similar trigger.", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Symptoms only when standing up", "Use of blood pressure medications, diuretics, or alpha-blockers", "Dehydration, vomiting, or diarrhea", "Parkinson disease or autonomic dysfunction"], "exam": ["Drop in systolic blood pressure of at least 20 mm Hg or diastolic of at least 10 mm Hg within 3 minutes of standing", "Heart rate may rise or fail to rise depending on cause"], "labs": ["Elevated BUN/creatinine ratio suggesting dehydration", "Anemia"]}}, {"name": "Cardiac arrhythmia", "slug": "cardiac-arrhythmia", "why_considered": "Abnormal heart rhythms can cause sudden loss of consciousness without warning.", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Fainting during exertion, while supine, or with palpitations", "discriminators": {"history": ["Palpitations just before fainting", "Fainting during exercise or while lying down", "Family history of sudden cardiac death", "Known heart disease"], "exam": ["Irregular pulse", "Murmur suggesting structural heart disease", "Signs of heart failure"], "labs": ["Electrolyte abnormalities such as low potassium or magnesium", "Elevated troponin if ischemia is the trigger"], "ecg": ["Arrhythmia such as atrial fibrillation, ventricular tachycardia, or bradyarrhythmia", "Conduction disease such as Mobitz II or complete heart block", "Prolonged QTc, Brugada pattern, or epsilon waves"], "imaging": ["Echocardiogram may show structural heart disease"]}}, {"name": "Structural heart disease", "slug": "structural-heart-disease", "why_considered": "Valve disease or cardiomyopathy can limit blood flow and cause fainting, especially with exertion.", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Murmur, exertional fainting, or abnormal ECG", "discriminators": {"history": ["Fainting during exertion", "Chest pain or shortness of breath with activity", "Family history of sudden cardiac death or cardiomyopathy"], "exam": ["Systolic murmur that changes with position", "Signs of heart failure such as crackles or elevated jugular venous pressure"], "ecg": ["Left ventricular hypertrophy", "T-wave inversion in precordial leads"], "imaging": ["Echocardiogram showing aortic stenosis, hypertrophic cardiomyopathy, or reduced ejection fraction"]}}, {"name": "Pulmonary embolism", "slug": "pulmonary-embolism", "why_considered": "A large clot in the lungs can cause sudden fainting with low oxygen and fast heart rate.", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Tachycardia, hypoxemia, or pleuritic chest pain after immobility or surgery", "discriminators": {"history": ["Recent surgery, immobility, or long travel", "Pleuritic chest pain", "Shortness of breath"], "exam": ["Tachycardia", "Hypoxemia", "Signs of deep vein thrombosis such as leg swelling"], "labs": ["Elevated D-dimer in low-risk patients", "Low oxygen saturation"], "imaging": ["CT pulmonary angiogram showing filling defect in pulmonary arteries"]}}, {"name": "Transient ischemic attack or stroke", "slug": "transient-ischemic-attack", "why_considered": "Reduced blood flow to part of the brain can cause brief loss of consciousness or focal symptoms.", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Focal neurologic symptoms such as weakness, numbness, or trouble speaking", "discriminators": {"history": ["Sudden weakness or numbness on one side", "Trouble speaking or understanding", "Vision loss in one eye", "Symptoms not clearly positional or emotional"], "exam": ["Focal neurologic deficit", "Carotid bruit"], "imaging": ["MRI brain showing acute infarction", "CT head may be normal early"]}}, {"name": "Psychogenic pseudosyncope", "slug": "psychogenic-pseudosyncope", "why_considered": "Episodes of apparent loss of consciousness without true cerebral hypoperfusion.", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Episodes occur only when observed by others", "Prolonged duration without injury", "No trigger such as standing or emotion", "History of anxiety or trauma"], "exam": ["Normal vital signs and examination during and between episodes", "Eyes may be closed and resistant to opening during episodes"], "labs": ["Normal glucose and electrolytes"]}}], "course": {"severity": {"mild": "Brief episode with clear warning, quick full recovery, no injury, and normal vital signs and ECG", "moderate": "Recurrent episodes or a fall with minor injury; vital signs or ECG may be mildly abnormal", "severe": "Fainting during exertion or while supine, with palpitations, chest pain, or abnormal ECG suggesting a cardiac cause", "critical": "Persistent loss of consciousness, severe hypotension, life-threatening arrhythmia, or major trauma from the fall"}, "red_flags": [{"finding": "Fainting during exertion or while lying down", "meaning": "Suggests a cardiac cause such as arrhythmia or structural heart disease"}, {"finding": "Palpitations or chest pain before the event", "meaning": "Possible arrhythmia or myocardial ischemia"}, {"finding": "Family history of sudden cardiac death", "meaning": "Possible inherited arrhythmia or cardiomyopathy"}, {"finding": "Abnormal ECG such as prolonged QTc, Brugada pattern, or heart block", "meaning": "High risk for life-threatening arrhythmia"}, {"finding": "Persistent confusion or focal neurologic deficit", "meaning": "Suggests seizure, stroke, or other neurologic cause"}, {"finding": "Hypotension or tachycardia after the event", "meaning": "Possible volume loss, bleeding, or pulmonary embolism"}, {"finding": "Major trauma from the fall", "meaning": "Requires evaluation for fracture, head injury, or internal bleeding"}], "complications": [{"name": "Injury from fall", "timing": "early", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "common", "clues": ["Pain, swelling, or deformity after the event", "Head trauma or loss of consciousness with injury"]}, {"name": "Fracture", "timing": "early", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Focal bone tenderness", "Inability to bear weight"]}, {"name": "Intracranial hemorrhage", "timing": "early", "seriousness": "life_threatening", "frequency": "rare", "clues": ["Head trauma", "Persistent altered mental status", "Focal neurologic deficit"]}, {"name": "Recurrent fainting with injury", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Multiple episodes", "No warning before episodes"]}], "special_populations": [{"population": "older_adults", "differences": "More often caused by arrhythmia, medication effects, or orthostatic hypotension; warning symptoms may be absent and injuries from falls are more common."}, {"population": "children", "differences": "Young children may not describe warning symptoms and instead appear pale, limp, or briefly unresponsive, often after a fall, pain, or crying."}, {"population": "pregnancy", "differences": "Fainting can occur from pressure of the uterus on the large veins when lying flat, from low blood sugar, or from anemia; it is more likely in later pregnancy."}]}, "teaching": {"key_questions": [{"question": "What were you doing right before you passed out?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Standing for a long time, warm or crowded room, pain, the sight of blood, or emotional stress suggests reflex fainting; fainting during exercise or while lying down suggests a cardiac cause"}, {"question": "Did you have any warning before it happened, like dizziness, warmth, nausea, or your vision dimming?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "A brief warning of lightheadedness, warmth, sweating, or tunnel vision suggests reflex fainting; no warning suggests arrhythmia"}, {"question": "How long were you out, and how long until you felt normal again?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Seconds to about a minute of unconsciousness with full recovery within minutes; prolonged confusion suggests seizure"}, {"question": "Did anyone see jerking or shaking of your arms or legs?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Brief jerking can happen with fainting; a sustained tonic-clonic phase suggests seizure"}, {"question": "Did you bite your tongue, or lose control of your bladder or bowels?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Tongue biting or incontinence points toward seizure"}, {"question": "Did you have chest pain, palpitations, or a racing heart before or during the event?", "category": "associated", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Palpitations or chest pain suggest arrhythmia or ischemia"}, {"question": "Have you fainted before, and how many times?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Recurrent episodes raise concern and suggest a chronic cause"}, {"question": "Do you get lightheaded when you stand up quickly?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Symptoms only on standing suggest orthostatic hypotension"}, {"question": "Have you been drinking enough fluids? Any vomiting, diarrhea, or missed meals?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Dehydration or low blood sugar as a trigger"}, {"question": "What medicines do you take, including anything for blood pressure, water pills, or diabetes medicines?", "category": "medications", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Diuretics, antihypertensives, alpha-blockers, nitrates, or insulin can cause fainting"}, {"question": "Do you have any heart conditions, diabetes, or Parkinson disease?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Heart disease, diabetes, or autonomic dysfunction raises the risk of a dangerous cause"}, {"question": "Has anyone in your family fainted or died suddenly at a young age?", "category": "family", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Family history of sudden cardiac death suggests an inherited arrhythmia or cardiomyopathy"}, {"question": "Did you hit your head or injure yourself when you fell?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Head trauma or other injury from the fall that needs evaluation"}, {"question": "Could you be pregnant? When was your last period?", "category": "obstetric", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Pregnancy changes the workup and raises concern for ectopic pregnancy or anemia"}, {"question": "Any weakness or numbness on one side, trouble speaking, or a severe headache?", "category": "ros", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Focal neurologic symptoms suggest stroke or another neurologic cause"}], "accepted_names": ["Fainting", "Syncope", "Vasovagal syncope", "Neurocardiogenic syncope", "Reflex syncope", "Passing out"], "reasoning_points": ["A brief loss of consciousness with loss of muscle tone and quick, complete recovery", "A warning of lightheadedness, warmth, sweating, or vision changes before the event", "A trigger such as prolonged standing, a warm crowded room, pain, or emotional stress", "No chest pain, no fainting during exertion, and no fainting while lying down", "No tongue biting, incontinence, or prolonged confusion after the event", "Orthostatic vital signs and a normal ECG", "Bedside glucose checked to exclude hypoglycemia", "Pregnancy considered in anyone who could be pregnant", "Red flags for a cardiac cause reviewed, including exertional fainting, palpitations, abnormal ECG, and family history of sudden cardiac death"], "difficulty": {"easy": ["Teenager or young adult who faints while standing in a warm, crowded room", "Clear warning of lightheadedness, nausea, and tunnel vision", "Quick full recovery with no injury", "Normal exam, orthostatic vitals, and ECG"], "medium": ["Older adult on a diuretic with a drop in blood pressure on standing", "Fainting with brief jerking movements that raises concern for seizure", "Recurrent episodes with no obvious trigger", "Mildly abnormal ECG that needs interpretation"], "hard": ["Fainting during exercise or while lying down suggesting a cardiac cause", "Fainting with palpitations and a family history of sudden cardiac death", "Older adult with no warning symptoms and a fall with injury", "Young child who appears pale and limp after a fall or crying", "Pregnant patient who faints when lying flat"]}}}$rounds_kb$::jsonb)
on conflict (slug) do update set name = excluded.name, primary_clerkship = excluded.primary_clerkship, clerkships = excluded.clerkships, organ_systems = excluded.organ_systems, validation = excluded.validation, review = excluded.review, profile = excluded.profile, updated_at = now();
